{"kind": "finding", "id": "F-recorder-events-028-01", "file": "Source/Parsek.Tests/BackgroundAttitudeSamplingTests.cs", "line": 20, "method": "ResolveBackgroundAttitudeMinSampleInterval_HighFidelityKeepsMotionFloorWhenMoreAggressive", "category": "T3", "severity": "Low", "confidence": "high", "falsifiability": "falsifiability: Source/Parsek/BackgroundRecorder.cs:4884; drop the Math.Min and return foregroundAttitudeMin -> red; flipping highFidelityActive in either cell -> still green", "what_it_asserts": "With highFidelityActive true, motion floor 0.02 and foreground floor 0.05, the resolver returns 0.02.", "why_weak": "ResolveBackgroundAttitudeMinSampleInterval discards highFidelityActive (BackgroundRecorder.cs:4877), so no assertion here can distinguish the fidelity branch the name advertises; both cells pin the same Math.Min in two directions.", "proposed_action": "Rename to state the Min contract (e.g. MotionFloorMoreAggressive_Wins) and add a mirror cell that flips highFidelityActive with identical intervals to pin that the flag is deliberately not consulted.", "effort": "S", "july_ref": "none"}
{"kind": "coverage", "sut": "BackgroundRecorder", "sut_file": "Source/Parsek/BackgroundRecorder.cs", "sut_line": 4869, "case_kind": "mirror-direction", "proposed_name": "ResolveBackgroundAttitudeMinSampleInterval_HighFidelityFlagIsNotConsulted", "sketch": "Call the resolver twice with identical effectiveMotionMinSampleInterval / foregroundMinSampleInterval and highFidelityActive false then true; assert both results are equal.", "guards": "Pins the documented contract that the caller folds fidelity into the motion interval, so a future branch on highFidelityActive inside the resolver is a conscious change rather than a silent double-application.", "risk": "recording"}
